-- #1617/#1618 BYSTANDER PIN for arrow- and effect-headed impls: unrelated code
-- must still behave when such an impl is present and never dispatched to.
-- `medaka check` reports exactly ONE diagnostic here, and the golden pins which.
-- The golden is not empty, so the fixture cannot pass vacuously: a cascade at
-- `println` would add a second entry and a lost diagnostic would empty it.
--
--   * `szc []` fixes nothing, so `Sz ?a` is an undetermined goal.  Its
--     candidates are the `Sz` instances whose heads unify with it: `Bool` and
--     `Int -> Int`.  The effect-carrying head `<Stdout> Float` is no third
--     type: it elaborates to `Float`, which unifies with `?a` as well, so it is
--     a candidate too.  Two or more candidates with no stable minimum is
--     `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE` (DICT-SEMANTICS section 3 Reject, section 6.2 T4),
--     located at the `szc` occurrence.  It is the shape of #2028.  Before the
--     candidate set was computed by unification this goal counted one census
--     tag (`Bool`) and was accepted, with `build` dying on an unstamped route.
--
--   * `conv 1` needs determination to find the UNIQUE `Conv` instance at head
--     `Int`.  The effect-headed sibling must not be a second match, or `b`
--     stays undetermined and a `Display` cascade adds a second diagnostic at
--     `println`.  A qualified head does not count against a concrete first
--     position (the bystander property of
--     `test/engine_fixtures/fun_head_impl_bystander.mdk`, which must build and
--     so carries only this `Conv` half).
--
-- Neither the arrow impl nor either effect impl is ever dispatched to.
--
-- Check-only: the `szc []` ambiguity is rejected, so `build` has nothing to
-- build.
--
-- The expected entry is the single `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE` for `Sz`.  The golden
-- pins `file:LINE:COL` (the `szc` occurrence, line 63), so an edit to this
-- header must keep the file's line count, and there is no CAPTURE mode: re-derive
-- the golden from a reviewed `medaka check --json` run.

interface Sz a where
  sz : a -> Int
  szc : List a -> Int

impl Sz Bool where
  sz _ = 7
  szc _ = 21

-- present, never dispatched to
impl Sz (Int -> Int) where
  sz _ = 5
  szc _ = 55

-- present, never dispatched to
impl Sz (<Stdout> Float) where
  sz _ = 6
  szc _ = 66

interface Conv a b where
  conv : a -> b

impl Conv Int Bool where
  conv n = n > 0

-- present, never dispatched to
impl Conv (<Stdout> Int) String where
  conv _ = "never"

main = println (sz True, szc [], conv 1)
